{
  "_readme": [
    "The envelope both backends have to agree on, byte for byte.",
    "",
    "Unlike the other fixtures here, this one is not a list of inputs and",
    "the answers one backend happens to give. Sealing picks a fresh nonce",
    "every time, so there is no output to pin. What is pinned instead is a",
    "set of sealed files — some written by Node, some by Rust — that BOTH",
    "backends must open and get the same bytes back from. That is the only",
    "check that catches a divergence in the direction that matters: a vault",
    "sealed under one backend and opened under the other.",
    "",
    "`refused` is the other half. An authenticated cipher is only worth",
    "having if altered files fail, so these must throw on both sides.",
    "",
    "`scrypt` pins the parameters rather than the implementation. The",
    "TypeScript passes none and takes Node's defaults (N=16384, r=8, p=1);",
    "if Rust used any others, every recovery key would be silently wrong",
    "and no test of Rust against itself would notice.",
    "",
    "Regenerating: see the note in src/main/crypto.conformance.test.ts.",
    "Run: pnpm run test (TypeScript) and cargo test (Rust). Both read this."
  ],
